- DO NOT repeat failed fix approaches. If previous attempts used a specific strategy, try a different approach.
- Use failed history as reference, not as automatic guidance.
- RE-DIAGNOSE the root cause, which can come from requirement issues. Previous feedback may have misidentified the issue. Analyze the current error context and code snippet independently.
- If the same approach failed repeatedly, acknowledge that pattern and propose a different strategy. Consider whether the persistent issue is in the requirements, not only in the Alloy encoding.
