[LESSON]: Alloy 6 does not allow a constraint that multiple processed requests in one step must have different processors unless you explicitly encode it; by default, allowing multiple requests to be processed by the same user is permitted if there is no uniqueness constraint on the reqProcessor mapping.
[LESSON]: Alloy 6 comprehensions (e.g., all r: Request | ...) can be used inside facts and assertions for group-processing logic, and absence of a per-request uniqueness constraint allows single-user group-processing as required.
